   987 000004BE 8D4C240C            <1>         lea     ecx,[esp+12]
   988 000004C2 8D54241C            <1>         lea     edx,[esp+28]
   989 000004C6 6A00                <1>         push    0                       ; lpOverlapped
   990 000004C8 51                  <1>         push    ecx                     ; lpNumberOfBytesWritten
   991 000004C9 6A01                <1>         push    1
   992 000004CB 52                  <1>         push    edx
   993 000004CC FF755E              <1>         push    dword [V(v_outh)]
   994 000004CF FF55AA              <1>         call    [V(iat_WriteFile)]
   995 000004D2 61                  <1>         popad
   996 000004D3 C3                  <1>         ret
   997                              <1> 
   998                              <1> ; waitk. At a console: WaitForSingleObject on the input handle for the
   999                              <1> ; time (EAX: 0 just looks, -1 is INFINITE), then ReadConsoleInputA for one
  1000                              <1> ; event. Only key-down events
  1001                              <1> ; count: their character, or for the left and right arrow keys (virtual
  1002                              <1> ; keys 25h and 27h, which have none) ^B and ^F. Anything else is passed
  1003                              <1> ; over, and the wait starts again with its whole time: so a wait can last
  1004                              <1> ; longer than asked by the time of the events passed over (a key-up comes
  1005                              <1> ; soon after its key-down), which the spec allows ("about n ms"), and no
  1006                              <1> ; clock is needed.
  1007                              <1> ; Input that is not a console (a pipe or a file) is read a byte at a time
  1008                              <1> ; with ReadFile, and only by a wait that is not just a look (a look would
  1009                              <1> ; eat the input); at its end the interpreter exits.
